---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Writing for International Trade — FusionMD & PolyWrite"
  description="A guide for Canadian government offices, exporters, and trade organizations: write in English or French, translate to your trading partner's language, and produce professional documents — with FusionMD or PolyWrite, on your own Mac."
>

  <div class="guide-wrap">

    <!-- Hero -->
    <section class="guide-hero fade-in">
      <div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/tutorials">← Tutorials</a></div>
      <div class="hero-badge">DataIsland Publishing Guide</div>
      <h1>Writing for International Trade</h1>
      <p class="hero-sub">
        More Canadian businesses and government offices are actively building trade
        relationships beyond the United States — with the EU, the Gulf states, Asia,
        and beyond. FusionMD and PolyWrite both let you write in English or French,
        communicate fluently in your trading partner's language, and produce a document
        at the end of it — on your own Mac.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-meta">
        Covers: on-device translation &nbsp;·&nbsp; multilingual writing &nbsp;·&nbsp; professional export
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Part 1 -->
    <section class="guide-section fade-in" id="p1">
      <div class="part-num">Part 1</div>
      <h2>Write in the language you think in</h2>
      <p>
        Draft the substance of a trade proposal, briefing note, or letter of introduction
        in English or French — whichever you write most naturally in. Both apps' spelling,
        grammar, and vocabulary tools work the same way they do for any document; nothing
        about writing for an international audience needs to change how you draft. Use
        FusionMD if the document is headed toward a formal publication or report; PolyWrite
        for anything simpler — a letter, a briefing note, routine correspondence.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Part 2 -->
    <section class="guide-section fade-in" id="p2">
      <div class="part-num">Part 2</div>
      <h2>Translate to your partner's language</h2>
      <p>
        In <strong>FusionMD</strong>: open the right panel → <strong>Translation tab</strong>,
        choose the target language, and click <strong>Translate to New Document</strong>.
        This is Apple's on-device Translation framework only — no fallback, no cloud service
        involved under any circumstance.
      </p>
      <p>
        In <strong>PolyWrite</strong>: open the <strong>AI panel</strong> (brain icon), find
        the <strong>Translate to</strong> row, choose your target language, and click
        <strong>Go</strong>.
      </p>

      <div class="callout-block">
        <strong>An honest distinction worth knowing before you rely on it.</strong>
        FusionMD's translation panel uses Apple's on-device framework exclusively — nothing
        is ever sent anywhere, for any language pair. PolyWrite's translation tries the same
        on-device framework first, but if the language pair isn't one Apple supports yet (Hebrew
        is one current gap), it automatically falls back to whichever AI engine you've configured
        in Settings → AI. If that's Apple Intelligence, you're still fully on-device. If it's
        OpenRouter, the text is sent to that cloud service to get translated. For official or
        sensitive correspondence in a language Apple Translation doesn't yet cover, FusionMD is
        the safer choice specifically because it has no fallback path at all.
      </div>

      <p>
        Machine translation handles most business prose well either way. For anything going out
        under an official letterhead, review the translated draft yourself or have a native
        speaker check it before sending — the same practice any professional translation
        workflow follows, just without the cost and delay of an external service for routine
        correspondence.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Part 3 -->
    <section class="guide-section fade-in" id="p3">
      <div class="part-num">Part 3</div>
      <h2>Or write directly in your partner's language</h2>
      <p>
        If someone on your team writes Arabic, Mandarin, or any other language directly,
        neither app needs anything special — macOS handles the input (add the language in
        System Settings → Keyboard → Input Sources, no purchase required), and both apps
        carry it through spelling, formatting, and export like any other document.
        Right-to-left languages like Arabic get correct text direction automatically —
        in FusionMD once the document's language is set in the Metadata panel, in
        PolyWrite via the writing-direction toggle in the Rich Text toolbar.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Part 4 -->
    <section class="guide-section fade-in" id="p4">
      <div class="part-num">Part 4</div>
      <h2>From draft to a document you can actually send</h2>
      <p>
        A finished trade letter or briefing note rarely stays a plain text file. Both apps
        export a polished <strong>PDF</strong> for email or a <strong>Word document</strong>
        if your partner's office requires one. If it needs to become a properly laid-out
        printed brochure or report for an in-person meeting, FusionMD exports
        <strong>IDML</strong> directly into Affinity or InDesign — and a PolyWrite document
        gets there too, with one click via <strong>Open in FusionMD</strong>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Who this serves -->
    <section class="guide-section fade-in" id="p5">
      <div class="part-num">Part 5</div>
      <h2>Who this is for</h2>
      <div class="checklist-grid">
        <div class="check-item">
          <span class="check-icon">✓</span>
          <div>
            <strong>Trade commissioner and export promotion offices</strong>
            <p>Correspondence and briefing materials for partners in markets you're newly building relationships with.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="check-item">
          <span class="check-icon">✓</span>
          <div>
            <strong>Exporting businesses</strong>
            <p>Proposals, product documentation, and follow-up correspondence with new international buyers and distributors.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="check-item">
          <span class="check-icon">✓</span>
          <div>
            <strong>Chambers of commerce and sector associations</strong>
            <p>Member communications and delegation materials for trade missions abroad.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="check-item">
          <span class="check-icon">✓</span>
          <div>
            <strong>Anyone who'd rather not depend on a foreign cloud service</strong>
            <p>For official or sensitive correspondence, on-device processing isn't a nice-to-have feature — it's the whole point.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Closing CTA -->
    <section class="guide-cta fade-in">
      <h2>One document, any language, still yours alone.</h2>
      <p>
        Write, translate, and publish — without a foreign server ever seeing what you
        wrote.
      </p>
      <div class="cta-links">
        <a href="/products/fusionmd" class="cta-primary">Learn about FusionMD →</a>
        <a href="/products/polywrite" class="cta-primary">Learn about PolyWrite →</a>
        <a href="/tutorials/fusionmd#t16" class="cta-secondary">FusionMD translation tutorial →</a>
        <a href="/tutorials/polywrite#t7" class="cta-secondary">PolyWrite translation tutorial →</a>
      </div>
    </section>

  </div><!-- /guide-wrap -->

</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .guide-wrap {
    max-width: 820px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem 6rem;
  }

  .breadcrumb { font-size: 0.9rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }

  /* Hero */
  .guide-hero {
    padding: 2.5rem 0 3rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--gray-light);
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .hero-badge {
    display: inline-block;
    background: var(--blue);
    color: #fff;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    padding: 0.3em 0.8em;
    border-radius: 999px;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .guide-hero h1 {
    font-size: 2.75rem;
    line-height: 1.15;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .hero-sub {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--gray-dark);
    max-width: 640px;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .hero-meta {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--gray);
  }

  /* Sections */
  .guide-section {
    padding: 2.5rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--gray-light);
  }

  .part-num {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--blue);
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }

  .guide-section h2 {
    font-size: 1.7rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .guide-section p {
    font-size: 0.97rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  /* Checklist */
  .checklist-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
  }

  .check-item {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    background: var(--gray-light);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 1rem;
  }

  .check-icon {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--blue);
    flex-shrink: 0;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-top: 0.1rem;
  }

  .check-item strong { font-size: 0.95rem; display: block; margin-bottom: 0.3rem; }
  .check-item p { font-size: 0.87rem !important; margin: 0 !important; color: var(--gray-dark); line-height: 1.5 !important; }

  /* Callout */
  .callout-block {
    background: var(--blue-light, rgba(0,102,255,0.06));
    border-left: 3px solid var(--blue);
    border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;
    padding: 0.85rem 1rem;
    font-size: 0.93rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 1.25rem 0;
    color: var(--gray-dark);
  }

  /* CTA */
  .guide-cta {
    text-align: center;
    padding: 3.5rem 0 1rem;
  }

  .guide-cta h2 { font-size: 1.8rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
  .guide-cta p  { font-size: 1rem; color: var(--gray-dark); line-height: 1.7; max-width: 560px; margin: 0 auto 2rem; }

  .cta-links {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    justify-content: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .cta-primary {
    background: var(--blue);
    color: #fff;
    padding: 0.7rem 1.5rem;
    border-radius: 8px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .cta-primary:hover { background: #005fa3; }

  .cta-secondary {
    background: var(--gray-light);
    color: var(--gray-dark);
    padding: 0.7rem 1.5rem;
    border-radius: 8px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .cta-secondary:hover { background: #e0e0e0; }

  /* Responsive */
  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .checklist-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .guide-hero h1 { font-size: 2rem; }
  }
</style>
